17:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"There is a well-observed pattern in hospitality: guests who experience a problem that is resolved well often rate their stay higher than guests who had no problem at all. That is not a reason to create problems, but it does mean a complaint is an opportunity rather than a disaster — and that how staff respond in the first minute matters more than the failure itself."}]
18:["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Step"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"What it does"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Sounds like"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Listen without interrupting"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Being heard defuses more than any offer"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Let them finish, even if you know the answer"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Acknowledge the impact"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Addresses the feeling before the facts"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"“Forty minutes after a long flight — I'm sorry, that's not what we want.”"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Apologize without blaming"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Owns it for the property, not a colleague"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"“I'm sorry” — not “housekeeping is behind today”"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Say what you will do, and when"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Replaces uncertainty with a specific"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"“Your room is ready now, and I'm sending coffee up.”"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Do it, and follow up"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"The promise is worthless without this"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Check back before the end of your shift"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"A service recovery sequence"}]]}]
19:["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Two things reliably make a complaint worse. Explaining why it happened before apologizing sounds like an excuse, however true it is — the guest hears you defending the property rather than acknowledging them. And blaming another department tells a guest that the organization does not function, which is a bigger problem than their room being late."]}]
1a:["$","p","4",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"When you cannot give a guest what they want, the technique is the same one that works everywhere: say what you can do rather than what you cannot. “We're fully booked tonight, but I can put you first on the upgrade list for tomorrow and I'll call you the moment anything opens” is the same refusal as “sorry, we're full”, and it lands completely differently."}]
1b:["$","$L1f","5",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"A guest complains angrily that their room was not ready. What should you do first?","options":["Explain that housekeeping is short-staffed today","Let them finish, then acknowledge the impact and apologize before explaining anything","Offer a discount immediately to end the conversation","Call a manager to handle it"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Being heard defuses a complaint more effectively than any compensation. Explaining first sounds like an excuse and makes the guest feel their experience is being argued with. Acknowledge, apologize, then act — the explanation, if it is needed at all, comes last.","optionRationales":["An explanation offered before an apology reads as a defense, whatever its accuracy.","Correct. Listen, acknowledge, apologize, then resolve.","Leading with compensation skips the acknowledgment, which is the part that actually resolves the feeling.","Escalate when it is warranted, but a manager fetched immediately signals you cannot help them."]}}]
1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Recovery is a script you should have before you need it."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write out the five recovery steps in your own words with a sentence you would actually say at each."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Rewrite these as what-you-can-do statements: “We're fully booked.” “Check-in isn't until three.” “That's not included in your rate.”"}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Recall a time you complained as a customer. Write down what the response got right or wrong against the five steps."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write a four-line response to a guest complaining about noise from an adjacent room at 2am."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
